From 9ffbb7bd31ce6dee774eb7f5ee565f006db8fc1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wmehanna <wassimmehanna@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:43:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] perf(tcg): keep TLB and jump cache state across ASID switches
 and TLBI

Makes the AArch64 softmmu TLB handling cheaper for a guest that
switches address spaces a lot, and fixes the correctness problems that
found.

- Keep global TLB entries across an ASID change and list the non-global
  ones that have to go.
- Range and VA flushes drop jump cache entries only where a large page
  is involved, rounded to target pages.
- Broadcast TLBI through per-vCPU mailboxes instead of stopping the
  world.
- Do not publish or keep a TB that read code a concurrent store
  replaced.
- Memoize aa64_va_parameters, skip the TCR2 checks when PIE and AIE are
  clear, take the regime of a PAC helper from the cached TB flags.
- Optional TLB counters, off by default.
- System tests: asid-retain, large pages from another vCPU (16K and 4K
  granules), range flush offsets, indirect-branch, jump cache key
  compares.
